    "archetype": "HIDDEN_MECHANISM"
  },
  "narration": "Your best decisions can produce your worst outcomes. That mistake has a name: Resulting. It quietly destroys fortunes. In 2015, one pass play lost the Seattle Seahawks the Super Bowl. Commentators called it the worst call in history. They were wrong. They judged the decision by the outcome instead of the odds. The hidden force is variance. Luck is just noise in the data. If you drive home drunk and survive, was it a good decision? Markets reward the lucky amateur and punish the disciplined professional. Over time, that incentive structure erodes real capital. Winners separate process from outcome. You evaluate the bet before the card is revealed. Stop judging results. Start thinking in bets.",
  "bgm": {
    "trackId": "bgm_dark_high_drone_01"
  },
